cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gaia DR3 NSS substellar candidate mining pipeline + tentative-candidate list"
message: "If you use this pipeline or the tentative-candidate list in your research, please cite the Zenodo DOI (auto-generated per release) and this GitHub repository."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Alejandro"
    family-names: "Zarco"
    alias: "alejandrozarco"
    email: "alejandro.zarcos@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/gaia-dr3-substellar-novelty-search"
abstract: >-
  An archival filter-cascade pipeline that cross-correlates Gaia DR3
  Non-Single-Star (NSS) Orbital and Acceleration tables against 30+ public
  literature catalogs and archival radial-velocity time-series. The pipeline
  identifies candidate substellar (13-80 M_J) companions to bright nearby
  stars that have not been claimed in published companion catalogs. After
  applying ~29 sequential filters (including conditional RUWE per NSS
  solution_type, HGCA Brandt 2024 chi-squared tier filtering, proper-motion-
  corrected exoplanet.eu coord cross-match at 10 arcsec radius, Halbwachs
  FluxRatio + direct-method M_2, both-estimates-stellar M_2 rejection,
  the Gaia DR3 documented false-positive list, and (v1.17.0) Filter #29
  Gaia SB2/SB2C double-lined rejection), the pipeline produces a list of
  26 tentative substellar candidates: 11 from NSS Orbital/Acceleration,
  plus 15 from the v1.16.0 multi-channel SB1 pool expansion
  (3 HGCA-corroborated: HD 156239, HD 156342, HD 11042;
  3 Tycho-Gaia PMa CORROBORATED-tier original pool: HD 343905, HD 199695,
  CD-70 5; 3 Tycho-Gaia PMa FLAG-tier strong-BD original pool: HD 83408,
  HD 153386, HD 221068; 3 Tycho-Gaia PMa CORROBORATED-tier widened-66
  strong-BD: HD 22782, HD 1912, HD 90072; 3 Tycho-Gaia PMa CORROBORATED-tier
  widened-502 borderline-BD: TYC 4291-119-1, HD 114124, BD+37 3282;
  1 HIP NSS-orbital x Gaia DR3 SB1 dual-detected: BD+14 4993 = HIP 115718).
  The v1.16.0 release also retrieved the full Hipparcos van Leeuwen 2007 NSS
  catalog (117,955 rows), which revealed HD 104828 has HIP Sn=7
  stochastic-motion classification - making it the project's first
  triple-corroborated candidate (HIP Sn=7 + HGCA chi^2=23.6 + Gaia DR3 NSS
  Acceleration9). v1.17.0 added an independent leak-free negative control set
  (24 stellar imposters labelled by the Gaia SB2/SB2C and APOGEE-SB2 channels,
  disjoint from every cascade filter) measuring out-of-sample specificity at
  0.33 (Wilson 95% CI 0.16-0.56); it exposed the absence of a Gaia
  double-lined-binary filter and caught one headline false positive, HD 76078
  (a Gaia SB2 stellar binary, K1=18.8/K2=17.6 km/s), which was removed (27 ->
  26) and the gap closed by Filter #29. None of the 26 are confirmed by
  independent orbital characterization. Status is experimental archival
  mining; confirmation requires Gaia DR4 (Dec 2026 expected) or new
  ground-based RV observations.
keywords:
  - "Gaia DR3"
  - "non-single stars"
  - "brown dwarfs"
  - "substellar companions"
  - "astrometric binaries"
  - "Hipparcos-Gaia proper motion anomaly"
  - "filter cascade"
  - "tentative candidate"
  - "spectroscopic binary"
  - "negative control"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
version: "1.17.0"
date-released: "2026-05-18"
